03:49:00.030 --> 03:49:12.670
Well Lucy did his doomsday, but he wasn't killed. He died of shock or ram. I wonder what those rascals wanted of him

03:49:12.670 --> 03:49:18.370
I think I can tell you Squire Trelawney. Now he's dead I can't

03:49:30.160 --> 03:49:37.530
That's my life. Doctor, Flint's map. How did you come by it, lad?

03:49:38.130 --> 03:49:41.980
Why, he gave it to me, sir, when he sent me for help. He said I'd share.

03:49:42.580 --> 03:49:43.240
Share what?

03:49:43.590 --> 03:49:47.400
You don't know. Pirate treasure man. Flint's gold.

03:49:48.160 --> 03:49:50.240
Why, everybody knows where the ship's Flint plundered.

03:49:51.380 --> 03:49:54.140
That fellow must have been the only one who knew where the treasure was hid.

03:49:55.430 --> 03:49:59.630
So that's what those scoundrels wanted, the map of Flint's treasure island.

03:50:00.250 --> 03:50:06.210
Latitude, longitude, crosses to barth the deposits, money to roll in.

03:50:06.790 --> 03:50:10.410
You're a trump, young Hawkins, mark by words you will share.

03:50:11.120 --> 03:50:16.810
Spidelass Hill, bearing south-southeast to finger-trunk tree, by Devil's Rock.

03:50:17.420 --> 03:50:18.800
Thence two cables south.

03:50:20.420 --> 03:50:21.260
Go on, go on.

03:50:21.660 --> 03:50:29.420
Bert and Albert, due northeast to foot of white crag, ten paces east, less seven.

03:50:30.190 --> 03:50:40.780
hundred thousand pounds my servants let's say come in tom redruth come in williams

03:50:40.840 --> 03:50:47.000
they got away sir they had a lugger tied up at kit's old sir hi you gave them a run for it boys

03:50:47.000 --> 03:50:55.550
they'll not be back thank you tom redruth thank you thank you sir

03:51:01.020 --> 03:51:04.980
Mum's the word. We'll take Reynolds and Williams along, make sailors of them.

03:51:05.250 --> 03:51:07.960
We'll have favourable winds, a quick passage,

03:51:08.400 --> 03:51:11.920
and gold enough to play duck and drake with ever after, eh, Hawkins?

03:51:12.340 --> 03:51:15.980
If you weren't so confounded exclamatory, Trelawney, we might understand you better.

03:51:16.600 --> 03:51:18.340
Just what is it you propose to do?

03:51:18.480 --> 03:51:20.480
Do fit out a ship, that's what I'll do.

03:51:21.170 --> 03:51:25.290
With a clue like this by Christopher, we'll have Flint's treasure if it takes a year.

03:51:25.770 --> 03:51:29.900
Can't you feel the deck under your feet and a good trade wind filling ourselves?

03:51:30.630 --> 03:51:35.280
A doctor can't go chasing across the world and leave his practice behind him.

03:51:35.320 --> 03:51:36.760
I'm your practice! I'm your practice!

03:51:37.690 --> 03:51:39.410
You think I'll put the sea without a ship's doctor?

03:51:39.900 --> 03:51:43.760
Besides, it's a risky business. We aren't the only ones who know of Flint's map.

03:51:44.300 --> 03:51:47.200
Those fellows who ransacked the internet are desperate men.

03:51:49.760 --> 03:51:51.460
Surely you don't fear them, Livesey?

03:51:51.910 --> 03:51:54.500
No. There's only one man I'm afraid of.

03:51:54.800 --> 03:51:55.480
Name the doc.

03:51:56.070 --> 03:51:58.250
You, sir. For you can't hold your tongue.

03:51:58.700 --> 03:51:59.900
Why? Confound you, doctor.

03:52:00.000 --> 03:52:04.130
After I'm no tittle-tattle, an adventure of this kind, I'll be silent as the grave.

03:52:04.870 --> 03:52:07.770
Now then, Harky, tomorrow I start for Bristol to find a ship.

03:52:08.160 --> 03:52:10.240
Once you settle your affairs here, you and Jim can follow.

03:52:11.430 --> 03:52:11.790
Jim?

03:52:12.050 --> 03:52:15.410
My Hawkins will come. You'll make a famous cabin, my Hawkins.

03:52:15.570 --> 03:52:17.490
His mother may have something to say about that.

03:52:20.720 --> 03:52:23.680
She'd listen to you, sir, if she knew you were going.

03:52:25.050 --> 03:52:28.640
Until I've made up my own mind, I don't know what I could tell her.

03:52:28.740 --> 03:52:29.980
Tell her that in three weeks...

03:52:30.000 --> 03:52:38.850
In time, three weeks, two weeks, ten days, Jim Hawkins will be sailing with the choicest crew and the finest ship's doctor in all England.

03:52:39.660 --> 03:52:40.200
Will you, sir?

03:52:40.360 --> 03:52:44.000
To be sure he will, boy! I'll wager my wig on it!

03:53:00.000 --> 03:53:29.730
Thank you, YouTube.

03:53:30.000 --> 03:53:39.080
journey. Abominable roads. The sea's the only high road for an Englishman. Come here. There she

03:53:39.080 --> 03:53:52.510
rides, Lucy. The good ship is Spaniola. Mutant. Out. She'll bring back all the pirate gold that we

03:53:52.510 --> 03:53:58.000
can put aboard her. There's no talk of treasure in a public place, I beg of you. Aye, Mum's the word. Jim.

03:54:10.780 --> 03:54:13.020
Well, Jim, don't you want to eat, lad?

03:54:13.460 --> 03:54:15.040
If there's time before we sail, sir.

03:54:15.500 --> 03:54:17.520
Sail? When do we sail?

03:54:18.020 --> 03:54:19.140
Better ask Captain Smollett.

03:54:19.700 --> 03:54:21.580
Five days he's been selecting a crew.

03:54:22.180 --> 03:54:23.800
Six men, all he's got to show for him.

03:54:24.180 --> 03:54:24.820
Cautious, eh?

03:54:25.100 --> 03:54:27.240
Cautious, he tries into every seaman's house

03:54:27.240 --> 03:54:28.600
like a judge or a quarter session.

03:54:29.400 --> 03:54:29.920
But I...

03:54:30.000 --> 03:54:36.040
to step in he told me to hire a sea cook so by job i did hire a sea cook right out of his own

03:54:36.040 --> 03:54:42.480
tavern fill up with the name of long john silver i didn't waste my time pouring over his credentials

03:54:42.480 --> 03:54:47.500
all the credentials i needed was a taste of his ham and his buttered eggs you can judge for

03:54:47.500 --> 03:54:54.260
yourself. Top of the morning, gentlemen.

03:54:54.720 --> 03:54:55.460
Ahoy, John Silver.

03:54:59.430 --> 03:54:59.970
Sitting down.

03:55:00.000 --> 03:55:02.080
the table's a star, but if he kindly will.

03:55:24.750 --> 03:55:29.980
You, sir, pipe in, ah, this be for Dr. Nets asking his...

03:55:30.090 --> 03:55:32.110
Pardon for bein' that familiar, but, uh,

03:55:32.840 --> 03:55:35.260
Skyery's told me so much about the two of me,

03:55:35.600 --> 03:55:38.180
it comes natural to call he by name it, too.

03:55:40.420 --> 03:55:44.760
And this will be young master Arkin's I'll be bound.

03:55:46.060 --> 03:55:49.140
Arkin's is a proper seafaring name, too.

03:55:51.180 --> 03:55:52.400
You run your house well, my man.

03:55:52.580 --> 03:55:53.820
And you keep a good table, too.

03:55:54.360 --> 03:55:55.320
Thank you, thank you, sir.

03:55:55.700 --> 03:55:58.180
It isn't often I see fruit in an English tavern for breakfast.

03:55:58.440 --> 03:55:59.860
It's a rule of Elf, I learn.

03:56:00.410 --> 03:56:02.450
while sailing under the Immortal Lord.

03:56:03.110 --> 03:56:03.770
Ah, rest it.

03:56:03.970 --> 03:56:05.030
You said that?

03:56:05.390 --> 03:56:08.890
That I just said, I was in 59 at Cumberland Day.

03:56:09.030 --> 03:56:10.550
When you shipped with the Admiral,

03:56:10.980 --> 03:56:13.410
never took surgery from the South Park and Art,

03:56:14.260 --> 03:56:16.980
not with a barrel of apples aboard for the men to chew on.

03:56:17.450 --> 03:56:18.790
No sense in that, Trelawney.

03:56:18.970 --> 03:56:20.330
Something we could profit by.

03:56:20.920 --> 03:56:23.260
And we'll buy again, there'll be apples on my ship, too.

03:56:24.260 --> 03:56:27.700
You favours the Admiral yourself, squire, if I may say so.

03:56:28.080 --> 03:56:29.960
Why, you and he could make up your mind.

03:56:31.530 --> 03:56:38.110
That he do, sir. I noticed it afore. It wouldn't surprise me none to where you say,

03:56:38.940 --> 03:56:41.880
Eve at the anchor. We sails on the hour.

03:56:42.310 --> 03:56:45.680
Can't say it without a crew. With all the hemming and hawing that goes on,

03:56:45.760 --> 03:56:47.800
you'd think there wasn't an honest seaman to be had in Bristol.

03:56:48.000 --> 03:56:51.600
I begs to differ, sir, if I may make so bold.

03:56:52.680 --> 03:56:57.690
Why, there's a full cargo of my own shipmates, assailed with Ork,

03:56:58.040 --> 03:56:59.980
be carved right here in...

03:57:00.000 --> 03:57:29.620
Bristol. Town men inside, if some of them was scarred in the service of England. And they with no pensions neither. Could a score of those foremost hands be had on short notice? Aye, sir, but they wouldn't be pretty enough for the modern taste. Nowadays they fixed the younger men by the cut of their jib, not the old ones for their experience. Appearances be hanged!

03:57:30.320 --> 03:57:31.680
Silver, get me those men.

03:57:33.020 --> 03:57:35.640
But it ain't a cook's place to must turn away hands.

03:57:36.040 --> 03:57:37.140
That's Captain's work.

03:57:37.200 --> 03:57:38.700
It's an owner's place, Mother Hokey.

03:57:39.250 --> 03:57:42.150
If you can bring in a crew of your stout-hearted dads come sundown,

03:57:42.510 --> 03:57:44.210
I, for one, will be greatly obliged.

03:57:44.470 --> 03:57:46.890
Well, sir, if tis owner's orders...

03:57:46.890 --> 03:57:47.370
Bully boy!

03:57:48.340 --> 03:57:50.960
But I don't like to be pushing a thwart my betters.

03:57:51.000 --> 03:57:52.800
But I'll say this, sir.

03:57:53.210 --> 03:57:57.500
I know every seaman in these here parts like the palm of his hand.

03:57:57.880 --> 03:57:59.420
Did you know Captain Billy Bones?

03:58:03.200 --> 03:58:09.510
Bones... Billy... What ship did he sail in, matey?

03:58:10.080 --> 03:58:11.140
He was a PILATE!

03:58:18.270 --> 03:58:19.890
Lord, lovely lad!

03:58:20.210 --> 03:58:23.470
Didn't you know that them that sailed with Admiral Arck

03:58:23.660 --> 03:58:26.280
Had no speakin' acquaintance with pirates

03:58:26.590 --> 03:58:28.370
Ness'n they parted us.

03:58:30.350 --> 03:58:35.110
Aye, Jim, you're the spittin' image of me when I was your age.

03:58:35.610 --> 03:58:36.970
Head full of pirates.

03:58:37.840 --> 03:58:42.810
But he'll find, same as I, that the sea be mostly hard work.

03:58:43.620 --> 03:58:47.320
And the biggest satisfaction a man gets is doin' his duty.

03:58:47.520 --> 03:58:48.460
Quite right, eh, Jim?

03:58:48.880 --> 03:58:50.240
Come to see, shall we go aboard?

03:58:50.680 --> 03:58:52.420
I just thought if he knew Billy Boat...

03:58:52.420 --> 03:58:55.120
Of course you did, of course he did.

03:58:57.550 --> 03:58:58.970
Beakin' your pardon, squire.

03:58:59.670 --> 03:58:59.970
Could he...

03:59:00.090 --> 03:59:06.130
Spare me the lad today. I'm more than my hands full, putting me in ship shape and rounding up a crew.

03:59:06.540 --> 03:59:08.540
Sound idea. Use 10 into my hand, Jim.

03:59:08.700 --> 03:59:09.420
But, sir...

03:59:09.420 --> 03:59:11.140
Don't fail me, Silver. Live safe.

03:59:12.520 --> 03:59:14.560
Come now, Jim, lad. Time be wasted.

03:59:35.150 --> 03:59:36.050
Down near me.

03:59:48.800 --> 03:59:50.980
Who are you, you old bumbo?

03:59:55.840 --> 03:59:56.200
Me!

03:59:58.300 --> 03:59:59.920
Ain't you the pretty one?

04:00:00.470 --> 04:00:03.370
swearing blue fire in front of a gentleman.

04:00:04.190 --> 04:00:08.540
Living up to her name, Flint, I cause her,

04:00:09.180 --> 04:00:10.960
after the famous buccaneer.

04:00:11.890 --> 04:00:13.770
Twas the pirates taught her to swear.

04:00:14.490 --> 04:00:16.410
Now, if you want to know about pirates,

04:00:16.940 --> 04:00:20.080
just you ask Captain Flint why she can,

04:00:20.180 --> 04:00:23.990
well, blow me down for an old sea car.

04:00:24.840 --> 04:00:26.780
Do you know any pirates, says you?

04:00:27.160 --> 04:00:29.320
Not on speaking terms, says I.

04:00:30.000 --> 04:00:34.580
The deer under my nose is Cap'n Flint, ha ha ha ha ha.

04:00:35.670 --> 04:00:38.250
I wager you can't make her talk.

04:00:43.700 --> 04:00:44.100
Cap'n Flint?

04:00:50.870 --> 04:00:52.530
You're a smart one, Jim.

04:00:53.120 --> 04:00:55.060
Smart as paint you are.

04:00:57.490 --> 04:00:59.910
Ain't everyone can make that bird.

04:01:00.030 --> 04:01:00.370
Talk.

04:01:01.240 --> 04:01:01.640
Neither.

04:01:02.000 --> 04:01:03.060
Glass of double rum.

04:01:22.580 --> 04:01:22.880
Damn.

04:01:25.740 --> 04:01:26.780
Did you say he was?

04:01:27.280 --> 04:01:27.860
Black dog.

04:01:28.620 --> 04:01:29.020
What is up?

04:01:34.350 --> 04:01:35.430
He was one of the pirates.

04:01:35.780 --> 04:01:36.880
One of them swabs.

04:01:36.940 --> 04:01:38.180
After him, all of he.

04:01:38.460 --> 04:01:39.440
Run him down.

04:01:40.190 --> 04:01:42.610
And if you don't catch him, don't you come back.

04:01:43.640 --> 04:01:49.020
What was he doing here?

04:01:49.020 --> 04:01:49.920
I'd like to know.

04:01:52.740 --> 04:01:55.420
Like him, they'll give my house a bad name.

04:01:57.640 --> 04:01:59.320
With the new landlords, eh?

04:02:00.090 --> 04:02:04.420
Why, he'd never set foot in the place again, would he?

04:02:08.180 --> 04:02:10.380
Doggy, I'll dog him.

04:02:11.370 --> 04:02:15.900
I never thought the day'd come I'd need this pistol against them cutthroats.

04:02:17.360 --> 04:02:23.140
Heavy ball and a light charge of powder works best on a touchy little craft like this here.

04:02:24.140 --> 04:02:26.220
Try the ballin'.

04:02:30.600 --> 04:02:32.640
See the engravin' on the trigger guard?

04:02:34.880 --> 04:02:35.740
Ollid Silver.

04:02:37.870 --> 04:02:41.170
Sir, a London made that there sidearm for Admiral Org.

04:02:42.180 --> 04:02:43.680
And the Admiral, he give it to me,

04:02:44.200 --> 04:02:47.040
a loyal service aboard the old Barton.

04:02:48.800 --> 04:02:52.780
Eh, do we think you could shoot him?

04:02:53.290 --> 04:02:54.250
Oh, yes, sir!

04:02:54.490 --> 04:02:55.550
All right, then.

04:02:57.430 --> 04:02:59.270
You are a smart one.

04:03:00.830 --> 04:03:09.760
I'd have known you could handle a firearm now putting in your pocket and keepin' there at Avcot.

04:03:10.470 --> 04:03:14.050
But don't go wavin' it in the face of every man who asks for a glass of stout.

04:03:14.320 --> 04:03:15.560
Oh, no, Mr. Silver.

04:03:15.720 --> 04:03:20.320
But if you clench your dead lights on that there black dog again, repel borders.

04:03:20.880 --> 04:03:21.500
I know, sir.

04:03:21.660 --> 04:03:25.260
And I know's a lad I can trust while I'm out doing my duty by squire.

04:03:25.880 --> 04:03:28.980
And when I come back, I'll have a crew and you'll have a pistol.

04:03:30.760 --> 04:03:31.700
You mean to keep?

04:03:32.370 --> 04:03:34.150
That's my meaning, lady.

04:03:35.340 --> 04:03:38.140
You've got the word of Long John Silver.

04:03:40.480 --> 04:03:40.940
Ship me.

04:03:42.460 --> 04:03:43.020
Ship me.

04:04:01.500 --> 04:04:01.900
I'm excited.

04:04:43.360 --> 04:04:45.340
I see you did it, Silva.

04:04:45.660 --> 04:04:47.500
Like I said, Mr. Trelarney,

04:04:47.660 --> 04:04:50.140
they paint pretty, but they knows the sea.

04:04:50.880 --> 04:04:53.240
Picked up horks old elmsmen we did,

04:04:53.820 --> 04:04:55.500
and a bosun what pipes

04:04:56.200 --> 04:04:57.160
Malawar fashions.

04:04:57.560 --> 04:04:59.480
Splendid, Silva! Splendid!

04:04:59.720 --> 04:04:59.820
Ha!

04:05:03.770 --> 04:05:12.510
Well, Captain, here's your crew. Would you care to have a word with them?

04:05:14.420 --> 04:05:16.020
Mr. Arrow. Yes, sir.

04:05:16.620 --> 04:05:21.040
Record the names and sailing records of every man-jack on board for entry into the log.

04:05:21.780 --> 04:05:22.480
And chalk your watches.

04:05:23.090 --> 04:05:25.200
Aye, sir. Get far out of there.

04:05:25.930 --> 04:05:29.910
And now, sir, I'd like to have a word with you in the cabin, if I may.

04:05:30.000 --> 04:05:31.680
And you, Doctor.

04:05:47.040 --> 04:05:49.070
Smollett, here's to our speedy departure.

04:05:50.100 --> 04:05:50.560
Thank you, sir.

04:05:51.320 --> 04:05:54.920
But I have something on my mind, and at the risk of giving offence, I'd better speak plain.

04:05:55.480 --> 04:05:57.640
I don't like this cruise, and I don't like the men.

04:05:58.320 --> 04:05:59.960
Possibly, sir, you may not like your employer.

04:06:00.120 --> 04:06:04.020
Stay a bit, Trelawney. No need for any feeling until we hear the captain out.

04:06:04.200 --> 04:06:09.240
I don't like secret voyages, Mr. Trelawney, when the only secret kept is the one in my seal orders.

04:06:10.050 --> 04:06:14.770
Everybody else about the town is saying that we're headed for a treasure island with a marked map to guide us.

04:06:16.180 --> 04:06:17.180
Someone's been talking.

04:06:18.140 --> 04:06:19.760
Well, I never breathed a word.

04:06:20.820 --> 04:06:21.700
Let's see, have you?

04:06:22.880 --> 04:06:27.580
In my experience, a venture of this kind may mean life and death and a close run.

04:06:28.120 --> 04:06:29.860
We may need a trustworthy crew.

04:06:30.570 --> 04:06:32.490
Not one recruited by the ship's cook.

04:06:32.860 --> 04:06:35.060
That ship's cook was acting under my orders, sir!

04:06:35.260 --> 04:06:37.260
Well, is the cook responsible for the ship's safety?

04:06:37.480 --> 04:06:39.860
Oh, really, I... I... I...

04:06:41.030 --> 04:06:44.640
We're all concerned with the ship's safety, Captain.

04:06:45.330 --> 04:06:47.590
As matters tend, what measures would you propose?

04:06:47.960 --> 04:06:50.240
Two. The whereabouts of any treasure maps

04:06:50.240 --> 04:06:53.260
to be kept strictly secret from myself and my mate, Mr. Arrow.

04:06:53.760 --> 04:06:56.680
The firearms removed from the forward hole and stored at here.

04:06:57.050 --> 04:06:59.170
Surely you don't anticipate mutiny?

04:07:00.030 --> 04:07:01.450
If I did, I wouldn't put to sea at all.

04:07:02.020 --> 04:07:04.080
The garrison arrangement's a sensible precaution.

04:07:04.660 --> 04:07:06.100
That's fair enough, Trelawney.

04:07:06.360 --> 04:07:08.230
Very well, if it'll get us out to sea.

04:07:08.600 --> 04:07:09.200
Agreed then, sir.

04:07:09.320 --> 04:07:09.500
Good.

04:07:13.110 --> 04:07:25.700
You'll find I'll do my duty.

04:07:30.320 --> 04:07:32.040
Hang it, Livesey, why do you take the fellas' part?

04:07:32.700 --> 04:07:37.190
Because I think our captains are very conscientious men.

04:07:38.140 --> 04:07:39.700
I find his conduct un-English.

04:07:44.180 --> 04:07:45.100
Downright un-English.

04:07:46.260 --> 04:07:47.220
Way anchor, Mr. Eddall.

04:07:47.820 --> 04:07:48.900
All hands on deck.

04:07:49.300 --> 04:07:50.100
And the windlass!

04:08:30.410 --> 04:08:30.610
Thank you.

04:09:13.790 --> 04:09:15.860
Captain, what do you say about our crew now?

04:09:16.500 --> 04:09:18.440
Ah, they're seamen of sorts, sir.

04:09:19.260 --> 04:09:21.080
Shades better than Lord Mayor's men,

04:09:21.320 --> 04:09:23.140
and no worse than dark wallopers

04:09:23.140 --> 04:09:24.460
brought aboard by the Press King.

04:09:26.500 --> 04:09:29.600
Mr. Arrow, brace your foreyard!

04:09:54.980 --> 04:09:57.700
I suppose you sailed with Admiral Hawke, too?

04:09:57.980 --> 04:09:59.900
Aye, sir. Master gunner.

04:10:00.440 --> 04:10:02.000
You brought your own cannon aboard.

04:10:02.530 --> 04:10:04.890
Men accustomed to warfare two-armed themselves.

04:10:05.480 --> 04:10:07.860
Not when engaged on peaceful commercial enterprise.

04:10:09.580 --> 04:10:11.950
Any further offense, twelve lashes.

04:10:12.310 --> 04:10:14.470
And that goes for all the folks who have.

04:10:14.880 --> 04:10:15.580
See you, Mr. Arrow.

04:10:15.880 --> 04:10:16.420
Aye, sir.

04:10:16.910 --> 04:10:17.390
Dismissed.

04:10:30.560 --> 04:10:35.510
Yeah, you ain't let no one see it happy. No, sir.

04:10:35.840 --> 04:10:38.900
I need to go hard with Long John if you was to turn it in now.

04:10:39.590 --> 04:10:39.890
Why?

04:10:40.340 --> 04:10:43.100
Well, here's a captain with a suspicious turn of mind.

04:10:43.420 --> 04:10:46.310
And here's Long John handing out firearms

04:10:46.310 --> 04:10:49.050
to an able-bodied seaman like yourself.

04:10:49.780 --> 04:10:51.080
But I'd do no harm with it.

04:10:52.440 --> 04:10:53.140
Getting out of sight.

04:10:53.640 --> 04:10:54.000
Yes, sir.

04:10:54.730 --> 04:10:57.370
You ain't giving to rum-drinking, are you?

04:10:57.940 --> 04:10:58.920
Oh, no, sir.

04:10:59.480 --> 04:10:59.960
No quite.

04:11:00.000 --> 04:11:05.690
Well, some, like some I could name, I don't want no meat pigeon on me.

04:11:06.410 --> 04:11:07.710
You shouldn't have crossed him, George.

04:11:07.830 --> 04:11:09.110
Now he can take away our rum russia.

04:11:09.230 --> 04:11:10.290
You knows his reputation.

04:11:10.550 --> 04:11:11.350
Now drink it all himself.

04:11:11.470 --> 04:11:12.730
Why did you give him that chance, then?

04:11:14.720 --> 04:11:15.680
You heard the orders.

04:11:17.050 --> 04:11:19.570
Seaman knives is all, and them in full sight.

04:11:19.980 --> 04:11:21.080
Well, it's real hands.

04:11:21.780 --> 04:11:23.020
Here's one he don't get.

04:11:30.640 --> 04:11:39.830
Ain't that a beauty now? Why, a knife like that'd bring down a gall.

04:11:46.140 --> 04:11:49.460
Burn me, John Silver. Don't he think he can come that over me?

04:11:49.900 --> 04:11:56.740
Time you learn, George Mary. Just who is Captain LaVargue this year? Commercial Enterprise.

04:11:57.490 --> 04:11:59.750
Captain as was, a captain wouldn't have that mate around.

04:12:01.180 --> 04:12:04.860
You lay a finger on Mr. Harrow and you'll answer to me.

04:12:05.220 --> 04:12:14.690
Mr. Harrow be a friend of Long John Silver's, and I plans to take care of it.

04:12:15.580 --> 04:12:17.700
Be that clear, George Mary.

04:12:26.000 --> 04:12:29.970
No, matey, if you and me was worth our salt, we'd think out of-

04:12:30.000 --> 04:12:59.450
way to sweeten Mr. Arrow's disposition. I knows what I'll do and dum-dum. My mother made that. Tasted proper on a cold night, didn't it? Did, uh, did your mother ever put a drop of rum in it? Good and strong, so the smell went up your nose. Aye, too bad we ain't got none. Dum-dum-dum ain't no better than Bill's water we outrun.

04:13:00.060 --> 04:13:01.120
Can't he get room for cooking?

04:13:01.320 --> 04:13:03.960
And have Captain suspect me a sneaking double drug?

04:13:04.650 --> 04:13:06.030
I could ask wire for some.

04:13:06.870 --> 04:13:08.000
Without Captain knowing.

04:13:08.320 --> 04:13:09.120
I'm sure I could.

04:13:09.760 --> 04:13:11.320
Blow me down so he could.

04:13:11.840 --> 04:13:14.820
You have any egress and regress to the gentleman in the cabin,

04:13:15.640 --> 04:13:18.280
but can you keep that many secrets?

04:13:20.740 --> 04:13:21.060
Aye, sir.

04:13:21.670 --> 04:13:23.350
Ah, you're a gun, Jim.

04:13:24.300 --> 04:13:26.000
I seen that from the start.

04:14:00.000 --> 04:14:00.640
Thank you.

04:14:39.690 --> 04:14:54.380
Plumbed up, I made a special re-user, gives him the fame.

04:15:00.000 --> 04:15:00.880
suit your teeth.

04:16:17.050 --> 04:16:22.560
Because I'm the one bought care of Mr. Arrow.

04:16:33.610 --> 04:16:36.690
And it shall be entered in the log that Mr. Arrow,

04:16:37.290 --> 04:16:41.870
made on the Hispaniola, was washed overboard in the storm

04:16:41.870 --> 04:16:48.050
on the night of May 14th, and his body not recovered for burial.

04:16:49.910 --> 04:16:54.070
Unto Almighty God, we commend the soul of our brother departed

04:16:54.070 --> 04:16:59.200
and commit his body to the deep men.

04:17:10.110 --> 04:17:11.910
Do you think we'll Eversight land again?

04:17:12.170 --> 04:17:13.180
We will.

04:17:14.060 --> 04:17:14.320
When?

04:17:15.160 --> 04:17:16.020
There are signs.

04:17:16.930 --> 04:17:17.210
Fun.

04:17:19.020 --> 04:17:20.220
Sailor's vapors, mostly.

04:17:21.670 --> 04:17:24.070
Crew always gets quarrelsome towards the end of a voyage.

04:17:25.010 --> 04:17:27.310
All the bears gone and the water cake's crawling.

04:17:28.590 --> 04:17:29.830
All you've got left is...

04:17:30.000 --> 04:17:34.720
Salt pork and boiled beans and boiled beans and salt pork.

04:17:34.980 --> 04:17:36.260
There's a few apples left.

04:17:36.480 --> 04:17:39.850
And when the last apple's at, we'll sight land.

04:17:40.130 --> 04:17:41.190
Then I'm going to eat them all up.

04:17:41.430 --> 04:17:41.810
Good.

04:17:43.030 --> 04:17:45.140
Hey, fetch me one.

04:17:45.360 --> 04:17:45.880
Aye, aye, sir.

04:18:06.490 --> 04:18:08.110
What do you think, George?

04:18:08.450 --> 04:18:10.850
We can tank this ship right now.

04:18:11.090 --> 04:18:12.330
Then what are we waiting for?

04:18:12.770 --> 04:18:13.970
That's what all wants to know.

04:18:14.450 --> 04:18:19.630
Since me and Norton joined you, the only crew left on Captain's side is Gry and Joyce and Hunter.

04:18:19.750 --> 04:18:21.590
Then I say, cut to our throats!

04:18:25.280 --> 04:18:28.620
And I say, there'll be no killing till I give the word.

04:18:28.780 --> 04:18:29.660
But come over you, John.

04:18:30.000 --> 04:18:32.200
When you were sailing with flint, it was cut and ripped.

04:18:32.500 --> 04:18:34.960
John's gone too genteel for blood-licking.

04:18:35.180 --> 04:18:36.720
You sick-headed swab.

04:18:37.290 --> 04:18:39.930
Who got rid of arrows so quiet that no one suspected?

04:18:40.440 --> 04:18:43.360
Not even young Orkins, who brought me the rum for the job.

04:18:44.170 --> 04:18:47.190
And who could eat firearms in the same way when the time comes?

04:18:47.590 --> 04:18:51.370
Nobody's crossing here, John, but we still would like to know what we're waiting for.

04:18:51.620 --> 04:18:54.760
We're waiting while a first-class navigator like Captain Smollett

04:18:55.070 --> 04:18:57.810
sails his ear bumble to our destination.

04:18:58.650 --> 04:18:59.910
We can steer a car.

04:19:00.030 --> 04:19:07.160
but who's to set one. You get plenty of cum rip when the time comes, but until I gives the signal,

04:19:07.400 --> 04:19:13.710
they too. Oh, we'll wait, but it won't be easy. Well, I wants them pickles and wine and a mask

04:19:13.710 --> 04:19:22.820
full of rum, I do. Well, the first is on ee. Fight into a Pippin real savage. It staves off the desired.

04:19:43.310 --> 04:19:46.090
I just can't believe it. I'd never have questioned his loyalty.

04:19:47.000 --> 04:19:51.040
Everything he told us was a lie. I've been a fool, sir.

04:19:53.420 --> 04:19:57.750
You're not the only one, lad. Captain Smollett, I own myself an ass.

04:19:58.400 --> 04:19:59.610
You were right. I was wrong.

04:20:00.160 --> 04:20:05.650
No moron than I, squire. I'm the man that signed Scully and Norton, and they've turned against me.

04:20:06.640 --> 04:20:12.340
There's just a few of us left now, counting Joyce, Gray, Hunter, Redruth, Williams, that makes us eight.

04:20:12.920 --> 04:20:15.460
Nine. Nine against twenty? Pretty heavy odds.

04:20:15.900 --> 04:20:17.820
We have all the firearms. Can't we surprise them?

04:20:18.110 --> 04:20:19.930
That's my plan when I get them all ashore.

04:20:20.660 --> 04:20:23.120
Did Silver give any hint when he meant to start the mutiny?

04:20:23.660 --> 04:20:24.060
Yes, sir.

04:20:25.060 --> 04:20:28.120
Well, here's my view. We've got time ahead of us, at least till we find the treasure.

04:20:28.220 --> 04:20:29.920
Yes, but can Silver keep his men in check there?

04:20:30.730 --> 04:20:35.630
If he can hold them back for 24 hours, I'll have every one of the mutinous dogs in irons.

04:20:37.330 --> 04:20:38.470
Well, here's our course.

04:20:38.970 --> 04:20:42.490
Play two, give them no cause for alarm, otherwise they'd strike at once.

04:20:42.590 --> 04:20:45.670
In the meantime, we'll arm the faithful hands and keep a sharp lookout for them.

04:20:46.280 --> 04:20:49.020
If you hear any murmurs against Silver, report to me.

04:20:50.760 --> 04:20:52.660
Jim warned us once, I wonder if he could do it again.

04:20:52.910 --> 04:20:54.630
Jim, could you play a part you don't feel?

04:20:55.080 --> 04:20:57.420
Keep your ears open and stay friends with Silver.

04:20:58.170 --> 04:20:59.130
Stay friends with him?

04:21:06.680 --> 04:21:09.250
Yes, sir. I'll stay friends with him.

04:21:19.510 --> 04:21:22.040
The sweet spot for the young lad ashore.

04:21:22.510 --> 04:21:25.010
You climb trees and a gulch, you will.

04:21:25.250 --> 04:21:27.570
And when you remind you to do a bit of exploring,

04:21:28.180 --> 04:21:29.960
just you ask old John and...

04:21:30.220 --> 04:21:32.520
He'll put up a bit of grub for he to take along.

04:21:34.850 --> 04:21:36.030
What's come over him there?

04:21:36.170 --> 04:21:37.950
Can't stop your dung there.

04:21:40.220 --> 04:21:41.060
All hand!

04:21:43.320 --> 04:21:44.720
Have you seen that land before?

04:21:46.060 --> 04:21:47.020
I have, sir.

04:21:49.280 --> 04:21:49.920
I have.

04:21:50.060 --> 04:21:52.760
I was cook on a trader as water, dear.

04:21:53.300 --> 04:21:54.060
Where's the anchorage?

04:21:54.180 --> 04:21:55.780
Yonder, sir, through that inlet.

04:21:56.600 --> 04:21:57.680
Can it be entered at Low-Tarden?

04:21:58.210 --> 04:21:59.970
Nar, there's a kind of...

04:22:00.000 --> 04:22:06.370
passage being dug there in a manner of speaking by nature. You give me a strong

04:22:06.370 --> 04:22:13.650
pull with a longboat, sir, and I'll guide her in like a lamb. Good. Stand by to load the boats.

04:22:25.640 --> 04:22:28.860
Come along in the boat. There's Captain Smollett.

04:22:30.000 --> 04:22:30.240
Yes.

04:22:30.890 --> 04:22:34.290
Young Arkin's ear wants to try his hand on a tiller.

04:22:34.730 --> 04:22:35.410
Submission guarded.

04:22:39.600 --> 04:22:41.920
Now that we've got here, what are we waiting for?

04:22:42.060 --> 04:22:44.600
We're waiting till I decide the time be right.

04:22:45.140 --> 04:22:47.260
Be that plain enough, George Mary.

04:22:50.010 --> 04:22:50.770
Lower away.

04:22:53.940 --> 04:22:55.680
You're to have the arm made sure of it.

04:22:55.740 --> 04:22:55.940
Aye.

04:22:58.800 --> 04:22:59.960
You read Ruth on guard there?

04:23:00.430 --> 04:23:00.750
Aye.

04:23:02.180 --> 04:23:06.100
When I give you the signal, jump on him so as we can rush the aft cabin and get them musked!

04:23:19.570 --> 04:23:20.780
Send mine away, come!

04:24:33.160 --> 04:24:33.720
Play two!

04:24:34.760 --> 04:24:37.590
Get below, you scum!

04:24:38.840 --> 04:24:49.410
Dash down the hedge!

04:24:50.060 --> 04:24:50.780
Now we're for it!

04:24:51.300 --> 04:24:53.100
Cast off the line and fall for the shore!

04:24:53.900 --> 04:24:54.340
Lively!

04:24:56.140 --> 04:24:57.020
None of that, my man!

04:24:58.210 --> 04:24:58.670
Turn about!

04:24:58.970 --> 04:24:59.390
Come alongside!

04:25:01.690 --> 04:25:04.590
Fire that musket, and I cuts his throat.

04:25:06.490 --> 04:25:09.380
Mary, you blunderin' squid, can you hear me?

04:25:09.760 --> 04:25:11.500
I, I hear you.

04:25:11.900 --> 04:25:15.360
Lie low till the treaty be made, and this time follow orders.

04:25:16.500 --> 04:25:22.040
As for you, Mr. Smollett, I'll give you one hour to send a boat ashore with flint snap,

04:25:22.360 --> 04:25:24.260
and give yourself up to Mr. Mary.

04:25:25.130 --> 04:25:28.850
So be it, you wanna see young Arkins alive.

04:25:30.830 --> 04:25:32.590
Open the door, lively!

04:25:36.870 --> 04:25:39.390
Aye, Joe, sir, we gotta save that boy.

04:25:41.600 --> 04:25:44.100
Oh, then, baby, don't he take it so hard?

04:25:44.850 --> 04:25:46.370
Why, he's lucky you came along.

04:25:47.140 --> 04:25:50.220
For old John here, he'd have had nothing to bargain with.

04:25:51.530 --> 04:25:54.450
But that don't be right arm here, your little head.

04:25:54.650 --> 04:25:56.230
Liar! You let go of me!

04:25:57.090 --> 04:25:58.210
There now, see?

04:25:59.090 --> 04:25:59.670
Here, here!

04:26:00.000 --> 04:26:00.200
Thank you.

04:26:45.130 --> 04:26:45.590
Fight, Dan.

04:26:46.570 --> 04:26:47.030
I heard him.

04:26:54.950 --> 04:26:55.950
Job at sight and you did.

04:26:56.890 --> 04:26:57.910
Must have doubled back.

04:26:58.850 --> 04:26:59.530
Kill the wood, mate.

04:27:00.030 --> 04:27:29.590
Oh, no, I have this.

04:27:30.480 --> 04:27:46.640
these five years will you ship name a maroon might that be flint ship no flint's dead sir

04:27:46.640 --> 04:27:54.720
that ship's a gentleman captain smollett gentleman says you flint's men says i i seen

04:27:54.720 --> 04:27:59.970
them some of them are flint's men but they got aboard by a trick is that i

04:28:00.000 --> 04:28:02.580
A man with one leg among them.

04:28:02.920 --> 04:28:04.080
One John Silver.

04:28:04.280 --> 04:28:08.400
Nay, if you were sent by him, I'm as good as pork, and I knows it.

04:28:09.080 --> 04:28:12.620
Oh, I don't understand. He's trying to take me as hostage.

04:28:13.180 --> 04:28:14.800
I hate John Silver.

04:28:15.000 --> 04:28:16.560
And fear him too, says you.

04:28:16.780 --> 04:28:18.860
Everybody feared Flint's quartermaster.

04:28:19.360 --> 04:28:21.520
It was him as marooned me here.

04:28:22.350 --> 04:28:27.880
I ain't had a mouthful of Christian diet these five years.

04:28:28.740 --> 04:28:29.820
Marooned by-

04:28:30.060 --> 04:28:34.940
and lived on toast and berries.

04:28:36.110 --> 04:28:40.610
Me neither, nor I dreamed of cheese.

04:28:41.790 --> 04:28:43.070
A toasting, mostly.

04:28:43.740 --> 04:28:46.440
You wouldn't have a rind of cheese about you, would you, now?

04:28:46.870 --> 04:28:48.830
There's cheese by the hundred way to board ship.

04:28:49.330 --> 04:28:51.170
Now, if you could help me rule along, Moat.

04:28:51.250 --> 04:28:54.310
Don't say you've been done your men, says I.

04:28:55.000 --> 04:28:57.500
What might you call yourself, mate?

04:28:57.900 --> 04:28:58.260
Jim.

04:28:59.220 --> 04:28:59.460
Jim.

04:29:00.380 --> 04:29:05.520
Jim, well now Jim, you just follow Bigger.

04:29:12.120 --> 04:29:13.120
A little more west, sir.

04:29:16.770 --> 04:29:17.310
There it is.

04:29:19.680 --> 04:29:21.940
With that stockade as a base for our operations ashore,

04:29:22.840 --> 04:29:24.620
we stand a better chance of rescuing that boy.

04:29:30.350 --> 04:29:30.830
That's all.

04:29:35.340 --> 04:29:36.260
Keep a sharp watch.

04:29:36.560 --> 04:29:37.760
One stem, the other stern.

04:29:38.420 --> 04:29:39.460
You'll be relieved in good time.

04:29:43.260 --> 04:29:44.900
Don't be afraid of those bilge rats.

04:29:45.490 --> 04:29:46.690
Don't underestimate them either.

04:29:50.070 --> 04:29:50.310
Travel.

04:29:58.420 --> 04:29:59.840
Keep that with me own hands.

04:30:00.410 --> 04:30:02.870
Out of bamboo and goat skins, mostly.

04:30:03.250 --> 04:30:05.190
And a trim little craft.

04:30:05.430 --> 04:30:07.680
Says you, will she hold us both?

04:30:07.840 --> 04:30:08.720
That she will.

04:30:10.360 --> 04:30:14.930
First, says you, we'll see if the coast is clear of Flint's men.

04:30:18.890 --> 04:30:21.760
No sign of them.

04:30:24.960 --> 04:30:26.510
Oh, sorry.

04:31:59.690 --> 04:31:59.870
that

04:32:00.000 --> 04:32:05.570
Captain a proper welcome ashore. Havar's pay no ee to him. Speak for the ship. We want them muskets!

04:32:07.720 --> 04:32:13.550
Now, matey, do you want John Silver to hear us?

04:32:13.770 --> 04:32:15.390
The captain won't know where I went.

04:32:15.570 --> 04:32:20.280
No need to. Ben Gunn knows where your captain's headed for.

04:32:26.130 --> 04:32:28.270
There be your friend, sure enough.

04:32:32.850 --> 04:32:42.440
If your captain wants to see Ben Gunn, tell him to come tonight alone to the top of Spyglass Hill.

04:32:43.180 --> 04:32:43.700
I'll tell him.

04:32:44.750 --> 04:32:50.780
And tell him them as hides can find, and them as finds can hide.

04:32:51.260 --> 04:32:58.710
Oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh.

04:33:10.180 --> 04:33:11.720
You're quarters, heavy George.

04:33:12.100 --> 04:33:14.530
I, I took the ship for you, didn't I?

04:33:14.770 --> 04:33:16.550
I can't remember asking him.

04:33:16.730 --> 04:33:18.250
You said when the time was right.

04:33:19.230 --> 04:33:20.190
Clap him in irons.

04:33:21.950 --> 04:33:23.090
Clap him in irons.

04:33:24.740 --> 04:33:29.120
Carry out your orders, John, but I'm speaking in open counsel for you to give George Mary another chance.

04:33:30.760 --> 04:33:34.940
George here ain't the one to lay plans, but if you aims to take this stockade,

04:33:36.850 --> 04:33:38.710
well, George is a good man in a fight.

04:33:40.040 --> 04:33:41.680
Too good to be rotting down below.

04:33:42.800 --> 04:33:46.900
That's very civil spoke, Israel.

04:33:48.400 --> 04:33:54.300
And now we'll put into Mr. Mary if I'm to take any more of his source.

04:34:00.370 --> 04:34:09.420
If I'm captain, then this is orders. All hands ashore, except Israel and Agathear.

04:34:09.910 --> 04:34:12.350
The two of you remain on board and guard the ship.

04:34:12.840 --> 04:34:16.400
If you're in trouble, you can signal me by firing the cannon.

04:34:17.360 --> 04:34:23.330
And when you're doing sentry-go, just ease off a point on the rum.

04:34:23.840 --> 04:34:25.820
Hear that, Agathe?

04:34:32.390 --> 04:34:39.120
Now which is it?

04:34:39.720 --> 04:34:40.860
Think or fight?

04:34:41.120 --> 04:34:50.640
What would you say, Jim, from what you saw of this Ben Gunn?

04:34:50.980 --> 04:34:51.540
Is he sane?

04:34:52.170 --> 04:34:54.340
Well, yes.

04:34:55.780 --> 04:34:56.640
I shouldn't wonder.

04:34:56.990 --> 04:34:59.670
A man who's been biting his nails for years on a desert island

04:35:00.000 --> 04:35:02.260
can't be expected to appear as sane as you or I.

04:35:02.440 --> 04:35:04.380
Why did he want you to come after dark, Captain?

04:35:04.900 --> 04:35:07.840
Safety, of course, but frankly I've no craving for his company.

04:35:08.040 --> 04:35:10.330
If he knows as much about the island as he says he does,

04:35:10.550 --> 04:35:11.590
I may pay him a visit.

04:35:11.730 --> 04:35:12.370
Later, perhaps.

04:35:12.690 --> 04:35:14.730
Right now, we may expect visitors ourselves.

04:35:15.590 --> 04:35:16.750
Can you load Jim Hawkins?

04:35:16.950 --> 04:35:17.510
Yes, sir.

04:35:17.900 --> 04:35:18.180
Good.

04:35:18.690 --> 04:35:20.750
When they come, we must have their rations ready.

04:35:20.970 --> 04:35:22.230
Let them come by Jove.

04:35:22.270 --> 04:35:25.630
They'll find me ready once I've had my brandy.

04:35:32.610 --> 04:35:35.930
Hold your positions. I gotta have a look.

04:35:37.980 --> 04:35:38.760
Flag of truce!

04:35:42.250 --> 04:35:43.990
What do you want with your flag of truce?

04:35:44.200 --> 04:35:46.800
Captain Silver to come aboard and make term!

04:35:47.530 --> 04:35:50.140
Captain Silver? Who's he?

04:35:50.430 --> 04:35:51.090
Me, sir!

04:35:52.310 --> 04:35:53.370
Poor lad dear!

04:35:53.950 --> 04:35:57.720
After your desertion, sir!

04:35:58.000 --> 04:35:59.960
My man, I've got no desire...

04:36:00.000 --> 04:36:00.860
to talk to you.

04:36:02.012 --> 04:36:04.032
But if you want to talk to me, you can come aboard.

04:36:04.924 --> 04:36:06.104
There'll be no treachery.

04:36:06.908 --> 04:36:08.028
Unless it's on your side.

04:36:08.316 --> 04:36:09.516
The word of a gentleman.
